WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
OSHA 10 is not optional. You need this to work on most commercial job sites.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
OSHA 10-Hour Construction Safety is delivered through CareerSafe, an authorized
OSHA Education Center. You complete the coursework online through CareerSafe's
platform and receive a DOL wallet card upon passing. The course covers the major

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Fatal Four: Falls, struck-by, electrocution, caught-in/between. Over 60 percent
of construction deaths.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Fall Protection: Required at 6 feet in construction. Includes guardrails, safety
nets, and personal fall arrest systems.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: OSHA 10 is required by most HVAC employers.
The DOL wallet card proves you completed the training.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: 6 feet is the fall protection trigger in construction. And
— Know the Fatal Four

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

